# Weapon_Balance — Skeleton

## 1. Applies when
Shooter or combat-heavy genres (multiplayer_shooter, tactical variants).

## 2. This document owns
- Weapon numerical identity: damage, rate of fire, range falloff, recoil/spread curves, time-to-kill tables.
- Cross-weapon balance budgets and counter-relationships.
- Balance patch intent log (what changed, why, expected effect).

## 3. This document does NOT own
- Weapon mechanics and feel (handling, animation, input) — Gameplay_Systems.
- Weapon acquisition/economy pricing — Resource / Progression.
- Weapon lore or names — Bible / Naming.

## 4. Recommended chapter structure
1. Balance philosophy / 2. Weapon roster & roles / 3. Damage model / 4. TTK matrices / 5. Recoil & spread / 6. Range & falloff / 7. Counter-web / 8. Budgets & constraints / 9. Patch log / 10. Open questions

## 5. Common boundaries
- Weapon_Balance vs Gameplay_Systems: numbers that make weapons *distinct from each other* live here; numbers that define *how combat works* live in Gameplay.
- One number, one home: a stat appears in exactly one authority; others link.

## 6. Common audit rules
- Every roster weapon has a complete stat row; no orphan stats.
- TTK tables are derived, not hand-copied (regenerate on change).
